## Geography (public domain)
- Natural Earth 1:50m (countries, land) via world-atlas@2.0.2 (https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/world-atlas@2.0.2/countries-50m.json,
  land-50m.json; ISC licence for the packaging, Natural Earth data public domain). raw/ (not in git); tools/prep.py builds assets/geo.json,
  gl_mask.png, af_mask.png.
- Projection maths: Web Mercator y = ln tan(π/4 + φ/2). Greenland's cut-out is a lon/lat mesh rotated ON THE SPHERE (along its
  meridian, then about the polar axis) and re-projected with Mercator every frame, so its shrink is the true Mercator scale change.
  Checks (tools/prep.py): Greenland 2.155 M km², Africa (without small islands) 30.00 M km², ratio 13.9; on the Mercator map at their
  real places Greenland covers 0.869 rad² and Africa 0.825 rad² (Greenland even looks a little larger).
  On screen the usual round figures: 30,4 / 2,17 млн км², ×14.

